cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below. It has not been refereed."
title: "The Erdős–Hajnal property for the six-vertex path"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "machine-qed"
version: "v1.0-proof"
date-released: "2026-09-27"
repository-code: "https://github.com/machine-qed/erdos-hajnal-six-vertex-path"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A proof that the six-vertex path P6 has the Erdős–Hajnal property: there is
  τ > 0 such that every graph on n vertices with no induced six-vertex path has a
  clique or an independent set with at least n^τ vertices. The proof is written
  up as a paper and formalized in Lean 4 with Mathlib; the formal result assumes
  three published theorems (Rödl's theorem, the Erdős–Hajnal property of P5, and
  the comb lemma of Nguyen, Scott and Seymour).
keywords:
  - Erdős–Hajnal conjecture
  - induced subgraphs
  - graph theory
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
